# Cloud folder → Mac disk

A project folder or GitHub repo created from Cloud Agent or iPhone must also exist as a checkout on the Mac, in the home folder, next to the other projects.

## Agent

1. After the repo exists on GitHub and `main` is pushed, clone it on the Mac when a self-hosted worker is available (`$HOME/<repo-name>`).
2. If this session cannot reach the Mac, do not ask Alessandro to clone. The Mac hook downloads missing repos.
3. One line in the reply: the folder is already on the Mac, or it will appear at the next Mac session.

## Mac

On session start, `deploy/check_github_before_work.sh` runs `deploy/clone_missing_repos.sh` (Mac only). That script clones owned, non-archived repos that have no local checkout. It does not move or delete existing folders.

Cursor chats still do not move between cloud and Mac. The repository folder does.
